  "blurb": "A recently renovated six-bedroom villa in a secure private estate above Choeng Mon, designed so the sea is in view from every room that matters — a 15 m infinity pool, a private cinema and a fully equipped gym, with 600 m² of living space on a 1,000 m² freehold plot.",
  "detail": "Inside a secure private estate on the green hillside above Choeng Mon, this villa was designed around a single idea: the sea should be visible from everywhere that matters. Long, low volumes of white concrete and glass step down the slope, and the seaward face opens completely — sliding glass walls disappear into their pockets so the lounge, dining table and sun deck become one continuous space that runs from the kitchen island straight out to the horizon.\n\nThe interiors hold their own against the view: curated art, sculptural furniture and clean architectural lines softened by warm timber, polished micro-cement and tropical light. Outside, a 15 m infinity pool runs the length of a 150 m² sun deck set against a wall of jungle canopy, with a covered terrace for a long dining table and barbecue, fenced landscaped gardens and room for a full-size table tennis table.\n\nRecently renovated, the villa now offers six spacious en-suite king suites, each with premium bedding, air conditioning and either a terrace or a wall of glass to the greenery; the bathrooms carry micro-cement through floating vanities, twin basins and rain showers. Beyond the bedrooms, a dedicated home cinema and a fully equipped, airy fitness room round out the house, with a laundry, two parking spaces and fast WiFi.\n\nHeld freehold on a 1,000 m² plot, it sits roughly 500 m from Choeng Mon beach with restaurants and cafés a few minutes' walk away and Samui International Airport a five-minute drive — equally suited to a family home, a private retreat or a well-positioned villa for rental income.",
